`citus_schema_distribute` assigns each tenant schema to one schema-shard placement, so `tickets` and `comments` for that tenant are colocated. Consequently, joins and foreign-key operations whose rows remain within the tenant schema can be executed locally on its worker. Shared row-based tables distributed by `tenant_id` are preferable when many tenants use the same table definitions, especially when tenant schemas would be unwieldy or cross-tenant operational management is required. With the same distribution key, related shared tables can likewise be colocated per tenant value.

